<title>USA: BEFORE THE BELL - Intel, IBM drop.</title>
<headline>BEFORE THE BELL - Intel, IBM drop.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Intel Corp and International Business Machines Corp shares lost support preceding Thursday's U.S. market open, the leading technology stocks under pressure from separate news developments.</p>
<p>Intel shares fell 2-1/2 to 145 in early third market trade in response to Goldman Sachs cutting its 1997 earnings estimate to $8.50 from $8.70 per share, traders said.</p>
<p>IBM was also singled out for pre-open selling, falling to 86 from 87-1/4, after it was reported IBM's chief financial officer Richard Thoman has left the company to become Xerox Corp president and chief operating officer.</p>
